altirraos-xl.rom -- AltirraOS XL/XE kernel, a drop-in replacement for the Atari
XL OS ROM.  Copyright (C) Avery Lee.  Distributed under the all-permissive notice
carried in the AltirraOS sources:

    Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification, are
    permitted in any medium without royalty provided the copyright notice and
    this notice are preserved.  This file is offered as-is, without any warranty.

WHY IT IS HERE: rsrc/atari-xl.rom is Atari's copyrighted ROM and cannot be
shipped.  AltirraOS can, so this is what a distributable image boots.  It is also
what makes an Altirra comparison apples-to-apples, since the emulator runs the
same kernel by default.

DROP-IN, VERIFIED: a 16K image of $C000-$FFFF, the exact layout xl_boot.c's
build_patched_os() expects.  SIOV at $E459 is a JMP it can re-point ($4C F7 E7);
the longest ROM padding run is 1433 bytes at $C670, far more than the SIO (~164 B)
and reset (~43 B) stubs need; and the checksum words at $C000/1 and $FFF8/9 are
ZERO -- AltirraOS does not self-test -- so fix_os_checksums() writes its delta
into unused bytes rather than corrupting code.  BallBlazer boots on it.

NOT a fix for the intro colour difference: the board still renders BallBlazer's
intro gold where Altirra renders it green, with this same kernel on both sides.
That difference is ours, not the OS's.
